error-state.summary:
Skills invoked: ariakit-general-workflow, ariakit-general-code-style (the remote is github.com/ariakit/visonaut; no repository-specific skill exists).

I reviewed the 5 variants of "Error state" in the explorer (1440 dark and light, width 390), each variant alone in dark and light, with data=today, brand=orange, radius sharp and round, and density compact. I also exercised them with Playwright (tab order, Details, copy, retry, focus, Escape). The builder's work was solid; I found one real bug and five smaller defects, and fixed all six. Lint and format are clean for the surface, and the type check reports no error in it. The page has no console error, no hydration warning, no focus on load, and no scroll on load.

The real bug: in status-chip, Escape did not close the popover on the explorer page, although the builder reported that it did. Ariakit closes only the topmost dialog, and a page with 7 open popovers has no topmost one. The cell now handles the key itself:

```tsx
const onKeyDown = (event: KeyboardEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {
  if (event.key !== "Escape") return;
  if (event.defaultPrevented) return;
  if (!open) return;
  event.preventDefault();
  store.hide();
  store.getState().disclosureElement?.focus();
};
```

Verified: Escape inside the popover or on the chip closes only that popover (7, then 6, then 5 open), and Escape in another variant closes nothing.

One copy change departs from the spec: the work line of cause-work-action for `stale-list` is now `Nothing was lost.`, because the spec line `The list below is 4 min old.` repeated the line above it. The change is in parts/model.ts.

The type check still reports 5 errors in files that are not mine: src/explorations/pages/history/ariakit/history-page.tsx:77, pages/inbox/ariakit/inbox-page.tsx:58, pages/pull/ariakit.tsx:141, pages/review/ariakit/loading.tsx:189, and pages/status/ariakit.tsx:92.

